#
# Larder, the household budget: layer 82 of the matrix. A monthly budget
# per category against what the owner's books say was spent in it: each
# category is a holder account of the books (ledger.accounts), what was
# spent this month is its balance now less its balance when the month
# began (ledger.balance), and the month's entries of that account
# (ledger.entries, those after the month's first) must add up to the same
# figure, or the answer is refused. Money is integer minor units, never a
# float; anything that does not fit is refused, never rounded or cut.
#
# Advisory and owner-confirmed: Larder never posts or moves money (it has
# no ledger.post). Setting a budget, starting a month and closing one
# (carrying what was left unspent into next month's budgets) each take the
# owner's word (larder_model.h LA3), and nothing is asked of zxvd without it.
#
# Built from an earlier layer: Coffer (73), nearest the core. A month's
# totals (budgeted, spent) are coffer.holdings, the exact sum in minor
# units (Trebago), and a category's excess over its budget is
# coffer.balance (spent - budget). The layer leans on no other layer's
# code. Understory (93) has over_budget (an excess of 1..18 digits), but
# it is built after this layer in the matrix order (place 92 against 87),
# so a use of it points outward and is refused; Larder's rule is its own,
# per category, and adds that a budget is set (0 is none, never over). No
# later layer leans on this one yet; its three entries are still general
# money rules, registered in CONCEPTS.tsv with Larder as their owner.
#
# Witness pairs are of one kind: what was spent is a number, in Sutra and
# Trebago (Sutra holds a holder's balance to 0..18 digits and refuses past
# it, Trebago answers: held); over budget is a truth whose fields Eve
# checks each against its own range, so the model gives it the excess
# spent - budget, and Sutra answers the same condition (an excess past 18
# digits: Sutra refuses, Eve says FALSE: held). The carry-over is an exact
# sum, in Trebago alone.
#
# The notify capability is declared for the over-budget notice, but zxvd
# has no method that raises a notice (notes.list and notes.mark_read only
# read and mark), so the model composes the notice's text
# (larder_t.notice) for the view to show. ledger.entries carries no
# posting time, so a month is the entries after the last one seen when
# the owner started it, not a calendar month read from the books.
zxapp 1
id     larder
name   Larder
version 1.0.0
slot   82
layer  L1
matrix 82
icon   icons/l1/082-larder.svg
budget 233
needs  ledger.read
needs  notify
model  apps/larder_model.c
use    coffer 1   # @num.coffer_holdings @num.coffer_balance

# What was spent in a category this month (LR1): closing - opening of its
# holder account, in minor units, one category per row.
provides category_spent num opening closing
logic    sutra   category_spent apps/blocks/larder/spent.sutra
logic    trebago category_spent apps/blocks/larder/spent.tb

# Over budget (LR2): a budget of 1..18 digits and an excess (spent -
# budget) of 1..18 digits.
provides category_over truth budget excess
logic    eve   category_over apps/blocks/larder/over.eve
logic    sutra category_over apps/blocks/larder/over.sutra
# Eiffel (contracts) and Solidity (contract rules) own this rule; neither
# runs yet, so Eve and Sutra stand in. PHP, also planned, owns templated
# pages and reports; no entry here is a report (the month's summary is the
# model's notice text, in C), so it has no line.
pending  Eiffel category_over
pending  Solidity category_over

# The unspent carry-over into next month (LR3): the exact sum of
# max(0, budget - spent) over the categories, refused past 64 bits.
provides unspent_carry num budget spent
logic    trebago unspent_carry apps/blocks/larder/carry.tb

# Its own proof (zxapp.h K1): each entry at its edges, and where its languages disagree
check category_spent opening=0,100,500,0,999999999999999999 closing=0,350,200,999999999999999999,999999999999999999 = 0,250,-300,999999999999999999,0
check category_spent opening=0,0 closing=5,1000000000000000000 = both
check category_spent opening=0,-1 closing=5,5 = both
check category_over budget=100,100,100,0,1,999999999999999999,-5 excess=1,0,-50,500,999999999999999999,999999999999999999,10 = true,false,false,false,true,true,false
check category_over budget=100,100 excess=1,1000000000000000000 = both
check unspent_carry budget=1000,500,0,300 spent=400,700,50,-100 = 1000
check unspent_carry budget=9223372036854775807,0 spent=0,0 = 9223372036854775807
check coffer.holdings balance=40000,12500,-300 = 52200
check coffer.balance before=350,100 moved=-300,-100 = 50,0
